@format 1
@id section-modification.reorder-section-by-drag
@title Reorder section by drag
@section Section modification
@area In Split tab
@entry row-press, mouse-release, capture-lost
@summary Reorder existing sections by dragging a row in the Split Sections panel; each live insertion that changes position updates section state immediately, while mouse release and lost capture terminate the drag UI state.
@related section-modification.common.apply-modified-state
@tag section
@tag split
@tag modification
@tag reorder
@tag drag

@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias ghost = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PGhost

[row-press] Section row PreviewMouseLeftButtonDown <input>
- A non-double-click row press stores the row, its current index, drag origin, and grab offset, resets drag-active=false, and captures the row panel mouse @ panel.PSectionRowBuild(...) / row PreviewMouseLeftButtonDown
> drag-motion

[mouse-release] Row-panel MouseLeftButtonUp after a stored press <input>
- PSectionUpHandle ignores release when no drag row is stored; otherwise it restores row opacity, clears the ghost, releases mouse capture, and records whether drag mode had become active @ panel.PSectionUpHandle(...)
? "A drag had become active" > dragged-release
? "No drag had become active" > click-release

[capture-lost] Row-panel LostMouseCapture <input>
- PSectionLostHandle restores row opacity when a drag row exists, clears the ghost, and clears all drag fields @ panel.PSectionLostHandle(...)
  @ panel.PSectionDragClear(...)
> drag-aborted

[drag-motion] Row-panel PreviewMouseMove <decision>
- PSectionMoveHandle requires a stored row/index/origin, no active inline editor, and the left button still pressed; movement must also exceed the system drag threshold before drag mode begins @ panel.PSectionMoveHandle(...)
? "Prerequisites fail or below threshold" > no-live-move
? "Drag threshold crossed" > drag-start

[dragged-release] Complete moved drag UI <process>
- Clear all drag fields, rebuild the section rows from current flow state, mark the mouse event handled, and return @ panel.PSectionUpHandle(...)
  @ panel.PSectionDragClear(...)
  @ panel.PSectionRebuild(...)
> drag-finished

[click-release] Treat press/release as row selection <process>
- Resolve the row's current index and clear drag fields; when the row is valid and is not the active inline-edit target, commit any pending inline editor and select that row through the flow @ panel.PSectionUpHandle(...)
  @ panel.PSectionEditCommit(...)
  @ flow.PFlowSectionSelect(...)
> click-finished

[drag-aborted] Drag interaction cleaned after capture loss <output>
= Temporary drag opacity/ghost/state is cleared. PSectionLostHandle does not rebuild rows or request another logical move, so any logical moves already applied before capture loss remain in section state.

[no-live-move] No reorder on this mouse move <output>
= Section order remains unchanged for this PreviewMouseMove; the captured interaction can still receive later movement, release, or lost capture.

[drag-start] Enter live drag mode <process>
- Mark the drag active, lower the source-row opacity, create a ghost at the stored grab offset, and keep the ghost synchronized to the cursor @ panel.PSectionMoveHandle(...)
  @ ghost.PGhostShow(...)
  @ ghost.PGhostCursorSync(...)
> target-resolve

[drag-finished] Drag reorder interaction finished <output>
= The panel has rebuilt from the already-applied section state, with drag opacity, ghost, capture, and temporary drag fields cleared.

[click-finished] Row click interaction finished <output>
= No drag reorder occurred; the release instead performed the normal row-selection path when applicable.

[target-resolve] Resolve insertion target <process>
- PSectionIndexResolve compares the pointer against each row midpoint and returns a clamped insertion position from zero through row count @ panel.PSectionIndexResolve(...)
> live-move

[live-move] Request section move <decision>
- PSectionLiveMove converts the visual target to an insertion index and calls PFlowSectionMove unless the row would remain in the same position @ panel.PSectionLiveMove(...)
  @ flow.PFlowSectionMove(...)
? "Same insertion position" > await-more-motion
? "Different insertion position" > editable-check

[await-more-motion] Keep dragging without state change <output>
= The current mouse move does not alter section order; subsequent captured mouse events may move again or terminate the interaction.

[editable-check] Section editing enabled <decision>
- PFlowSectionMove rejects the request when section editing is disabled; otherwise it calls LSegmentMove @ flow.PFlowSectionMove(...)
? "Editing disabled" > move-rejected
? "Editing enabled" > move-plan

[move-rejected] Reorder rejected <output>
= The logical section order and visual row order remain unchanged for this mouse move.

[move-plan] Compute logical insertion <decision>
- LSegmentMove validates the original source index, adjusts the requested target for removal of the source row, clamps it, and rejects a no-op insertion @ segment.LSegmentMove(...)
? "Invalid source or computed no-op" > logical-noop
? "Valid new insertion" > reorder-list

[logical-noop] No logical move <output>
= PFlowSectionMove returns false and the panel does not move the row for this mouse event.

[reorder-list] Reorder pieces and preserve selection semantics <process>
- Remove the source LPiece and insert it at the computed index; if that source section was selected, move the active index with it, otherwise keep the existing numeric active index unchanged @ segment.LSegmentMove(...)
> map:section-modification.common.apply-modified-state
